TESTSUITE "CHKCLR"

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> A note on how these test cases are shaped:
*>
*> 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS' six early-return guards (routing invalid, account
*> not found, SQL error, closed account, stop payment, NSF) all end with
*> "PERFORM 2800-WRITE-RETURN / PERFORM 1100-READ-CHECK / GO TO
*> 2000-EXIT". Because the driving PERFORM in 0000-MAIN-PROCESS
*> ("PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS UNTIL WS-CHK-FILE-EOF") never says
*> "THRU 2000-EXIT", GO TO jumps past the compiler-inserted return point
*> for a plain "PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS" call: real GnuCOBOL falls
*> through 2000-EXIT into 2800-WRITE-RETURN a second time (duplicating
*> the return record) and then into 3000-FINALIZE (COMMIT/CLOSE/
*> RETURN-CODE) before finally returning. That is real, verified runtime
*> behavior of this source file (confirmed against the mockymock-cobc
*> GnuCOBOL toolchain), not a test artifact -- see the write-up at the
*> bottom of this file. The six early-return TESTCASEs below drive
*> "PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE" (mocking every
*> boundary that chain really reaches, including CLOSE) so the test can
*> observe the guard's own business outcome without the run crashing on
*> an unmocked CLOSE of files that were never opened in an isolated
*> paragraph test. The cleared/happy-path and posting-failure cases never
*> hit a GO TO, so a plain "PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS" is faithful to
*> the real control flow for them.
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

*> Happy path: routing validates, the account is open with enough
*> available balance, there's no stop payment on file, and both the
*> INSERT and UPDATE succeed -- the check clears and the ledger balance
*> is debited.
TESTCASE "cleared check posts a debit and updates the account"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE "A" TO HV-ACCT-STATUS
        MOVE 5000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
        MOVE 5000.00 TO HV-AVAILABLE-BALANCE
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000001"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000001"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 250.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS
    EXPECT WS-ITEMS-CLEARED TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL-CLEARED TO BE 250.00
    EXPECT WS-CHK-ERRORS TO BE 0
    EXPECT WS-CD-STATUS TO BE "CLEARED"
    VERIFY CALL "ACCTVAL" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "SELECT" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "COMMIT" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY SQL "ROLLBACK" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY WRITE RETURN-RECORD WAS CALLED NEVER
    *> Real behavior of this source, not a test gap: a bare "PERFORM
    *> 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS" returns at the compiler-inserted boundary
    *> right before 2000-EXIT, so 1100-READ-CHECK's READ CHKFILE never
    *> fires on the cleared path -- see the note at the top of this file.
    VERIFY READ CHKFILE WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Same happy-path setup, but the INSERT into TRANSACTION_HIST fails at
*> the database. The program rolls back and bumps the error counter --
*> but note it still unconditionally reports the item as "CLEARED" on
*> the run report and never calls UPDATE, since that MOVE/WRITE sequence
*> isn't guarded by the SQLCODE check above it.
TESTCASE "SQL error during posting is rolled back and not counted as cleared"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE "A" TO HV-ACCT-STATUS
        MOVE 5000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
        MOVE 5000.00 TO HV-AVAILABLE-BALANCE
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE -911 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000008"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000008"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 250.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS
    EXPECT WS-CHK-ERRORS TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-ITEMS-CLEARED TO BE 0
    EXPECT WS-CD-STATUS TO BE "CLEARED"
    VERIFY SQL "ROLLBACK" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY SQL "COMMIT" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Routing number fails ACCTVAL's 'R' (routing) check -- returned R06
*> before the account is ever looked up in DB2.
TESTCASE "invalid routing number is returned as R06 without an account lookup"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "N" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE "A" TO HV-ACCT-STATUS
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "999999999"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000002"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000002"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 100.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT WS-RETURN-REASON TO BE "R06"
    EXPECT WS-ROUTING-INVALID TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-CHK-ERRORS TO BE 0
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0
    VERIFY CALL "ACCTVAL" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "SELECT" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> DB2 finds no row for the account (SQLCODE +100) -- returned R03.
TESTCASE "account not found in DB2 is returned as R03 without a stop-pay check"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE 100 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00009999"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000003"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 100.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT WS-RETURN-REASON TO BE "R03"
    EXPECT WS-ITEMS-CLOSED TO BE 1
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0
    VERIFY READ STOPPAY WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Any other DB2 failure (deadlock, resource unavailable, etc.) during
*> the account lookup is a hard error: the item is skipped, WS-CHK-ERRORS
*> is bumped (driving RETURN-CODE 4 at end of run), and -- unlike the
*> other five guards -- 2800-WRITE-RETURN is never PERFORMed directly on
*> this branch (no WS-RETURN-REASON is set either), so the one return
*> record that gets written comes solely from the GO TO 2000-EXIT
*> fall-through, not a normal guard write.
TESTCASE "unexpected SQL error during account lookup counts as a hard error"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE -818 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000004"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000004"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 100.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT WS-CHK-ERRORS TO BE 1
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 4
    VERIFY READ STOPPAY WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY WRITE RETURN-RECORD WAS CALLED ONCE

*> Account is found but flagged closed ('C') -- returned R02, again
*> without ever consulting the stop-payment file.
TESTCASE "closed account is returned as R02"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE "C" TO HV-ACCT-STATUS
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000005"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000005"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 100.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT WS-RETURN-REASON TO BE "R02"
    EXPECT WS-ITEMS-CLOSED TO BE 1
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0
    VERIFY READ STOPPAY WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Account is open and has plenty of available balance, but the
*> account/check-number pair has an active stop payment on file --
*> returned R08 before the funds-availability check ever runs.
TESTCASE "stop payment on file is returned as R08"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE "A" TO HV-ACCT-STATUS
        MOVE 5000.00 TO HV-AVAILABLE-BALANCE
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "00" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000006"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000006"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 500.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT WS-RETURN-REASON TO BE "R08"
    EXPECT WS-ITEMS-STOPPED TO BE 1
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "INSERT" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Account is open, not stopped, but the available balance is less than
*> the check amount -- returned R01 (NSF) and the ledger is never
*> touched (no INSERT/UPDATE).
TESTCASE "insufficient funds is returned as R01 without posting a debit"
    MOCK CALL "ACCTVAL"
        MOVE "V" TO WS-AV-RESULT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "SELECT"
        MOVE "A" TO HV-ACCT-STATUS
        MOVE 50.00 TO HV-AVAILABLE-BALANCE
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ STOPPAY
        MOVE "23" TO WS-SP-STATUS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RETURN-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "021000021"     TO CHK-ROUTING-NUMBER
    MOVE "ACCT00000007"  TO CHK-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "CHK0000007"    TO CHK-CHECK-NUMBER
    MOVE 500.00           TO CHK-AMOUNT
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT WS-RETURN-REASON TO BE "R01"
    EXPECT WS-ITEMS-NSF TO BE 1
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "INSERT" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> 1000-INITIALIZE builds WS-BUSINESS-DATE from FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE,
*> opens all four files, writes the report header, and primes the first
*> read.
TESTCASE "1000-INITIALIZE opens files and primes the first read"
    MOCK OPEN CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK OPEN STOPPAY
    END-MOCK
    MOCK OPEN CHKRETURNS
    END-MOCK
    MOCK OPEN CHKRPT
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK READ CHKFILE
        SET WS-CHK-FILE-EOF TO TRUE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM 1000-INITIALIZE
    EXPECT WS-BUSINESS-DATE TO BE "2026-08-08"
    VERIFY OPEN CHKFILE WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY OPEN STOPPAY WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY OPEN CHKRETURNS WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY OPEN CHKRPT WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY READ CHKFILE WAS CALLED ONCE

*> 3000-FINALIZE surfaces a nonzero RETURN-CODE to the JCL step whenever
*> any item hit a hard processing error during the run.
TESTCASE "3000-FINALIZE signals failure to the caller when errors occurred"
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 3 TO WS-CHK-ERRORS
    PERFORM 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 4

*> ...and reports success (RETURN-CODE 0) when the run had none.
TESTCASE "3000-FINALIZE signals success when no errors occurred"
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE CHKFILE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> Source bugs found while writing this suite (see the top-of-file note
*> for the runtime evidence):
*>
*> 1. FIXED (both this copy and the legacy-application canonical copy):
*>    WORKING-STORAGE declared two data items sharing the literal name
*>    WS-CHK-EOF -- the 88-level "88 WS-CHK-EOF VALUE '10'." under
*>    WS-CHK-STATUS, and the unrelated top-level EOF flag "01 WS-CHK-EOF
*>    PIC X(01)". Neither the program itself nor this suite ever
*>    references the bare name (the program always qualifies via
*>    WS-CHK-FILE-EOF), but mockymock's own generated
*>    UT-RESET-WORKING-STORAGE paragraph does reset every VALUE'd field
*>    by name and hit "'WS-CHK-EOF' is ambiguous" from GnuCOBOL. Renamed
*>    the dead, never-referenced 88-level to WS-CHK-STATUS-EOF.
*> 2. FIXED (both copies): "WRITE RPT-RECORD FROM WS-CHK-DETAIL" at the
*>    end of 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS had no terminating period before the
*>    "2000-EXIT." paragraph header, leaving the entire IF/EVALUATE tree
*>    above it as one unterminated sentence -- GnuCOBOL failed to parse
*>    "2000-EXIT" as a paragraph name once anything was spliced into
*>    that tree. Added the missing period.
*> 3. NOT FIXED (out of scope -- a control-flow bug, not a compile
*>    blocker, and off limits per the task's business-logic constraint):
*>    0000-MAIN-PROCESS drives the loop with "PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS
*>    UNTIL WS-CHK-FILE-EOF" -- missing "THRU 2000-EXIT". Verified against
*>    the real GnuCOBOL toolchain: a bare PERFORM of 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS
*>    returns at the compiler-inserted boundary *before* 2000-EXIT, so on
*>    a CLEARED check 1100-READ-CHECK's READ CHKFILE never fires -- the
*>    file position never advances (the loop would spin on the same
*>    record forever). On any of the six GO TO 2000-EXIT paths, the GOTO
*>    jumps past that same boundary and falls all the way through
*>    2000-EXIT -> 2800-WRITE-RETURN (a second, duplicate return-record
*>    write) -> 3000-FINALIZE (COMMIT/CLOSE/RETURN-CODE) -> end of
*>    PROCEDURE DIVISION, terminating the whole batch job after just one
*>    item. As written, this program cannot correctly process a
*>    multi-record CHKFILE. The intended fix would be
*>    "PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-CHECKS THRU 2000-EXIT UNTIL WS-CHK-FILE-EOF".
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
